<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Eritrean War of Independence</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1961">1961</a>–<a href="/years/1991">1991</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Eritrean War of Independence was a thirty-year struggle by Eritrean nationalist fronts against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopia">Ethiopia</a>, which had annexed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eritrea">Eritrea</a> in 1962. Begun by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eritrean-liberation-front">Eritrean Liberation Front</a> in 1961, it was carried to victory by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eritrean-peoples-liberation-front">Eritrean People's Liberation Front</a>, which took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asmara">Asmara</a> in May 1991 as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/derg">Derg</a> regime collapsed. Eritrea became formally independent after a referendum in 1993.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/eritrean-war-of-independence.jpg" alt="Eritrean War of Independence" width="320" height="263" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Skilla1st · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Eritrean_Independence_War_Map.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
